,1585,1586],{"class":55,"line":662},[53,1587,205],{"class":67},[19,1589,1590,1591,75,1593,75,1595,1597,1598,1601,1602,1605],{},"Every intermediate component (",[23,1592,1435],{},[23,1594,1469],{},[23,1596,1501],{},") now has an irrelevant prop in its signature purely as a pass-through, and adding a second cross-cutting value means touching every layer again. Two real solutions exist: ",[28,1599,1600],{},"composition"," (pass the already-built element down instead of raw data — see chapter 15) or ",[28,1603,1604],{},"Context"," (chapter 7), which lets any descendant read a value without every layer forwarding it. This chapter only names the problem; the next chapters build the tools that solve it.",[14,1607,1609],{"id":1608},"component-naming-and-file-organization","Component Naming and File Organization",[41,1611,1613],{"language":1612},"bash",[45,1614,1617],{"className":1615,"code":1616,"language":1612,"meta":49,"style":49},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","# Convention: one component per file, filename matches the component name\nsrc\u002Fcomponents\u002F\n├── UserCard.jsx\n├── Button.jsx\n└── Card.jsx\n",[23,1618,1619,1624,1629,1637,1644],{"__ignoreMap":49},[53,1620,1621],{"class":55,"line":56},[53,1622,1623],{"class":395},"# Convention: one component per file, filename matches the component name\n",[53,1625,1626],{"class":55,"line":89},[53,1627,1628],{"class":63},"src\u002Fcomponents\u002F\n",[53,1630,1631,1634],{"class":55,"line":98},[53,1632,1633],{"class":63},"├──",[53,1635,1636],{"class":114}," UserCard.jsx\n",[53,1638,1639,1641],{"class":55,"line":121},[53,1640,1633],{"class":63},[53,1642,1643],{"class":114}," Button.jsx\n",[53,1645,1646,1649],{"class":55,"line":157},[53,1647,1648],{"class":63},"└──",[53,1650,1651],{"class":114}," Card.jsx\n",[14,1653,1655],{"id":1654},"proptypes-runtime-validation-pre-typescript-era","PropTypes (Runtime Validation, Pre-TypeScript Era)",[19,1657,1658,1659,1662],{},"Before TypeScript was the default recommendation (chapter 23), teams used the ",[23,1660,1661],{},"prop-types"," package for runtime prop validation in plain JavaScript projects. It's still seen in legacy and TS-free codebases.",[41,1664,1665],{"language":43},[45,1666,1668],{"className":47,"code":1667,"language":43,"meta":49,"style":49},"import PropTypes from 'prop-types'\n\nfunction UserCard({ name, age }) {\n  return \u003Cp>{name} is {age}\u003C\u002Fp>\n}\n\nUserCard.propTypes = {\n  name: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n  age: PropTypes.number,\n}\n\u002F\u002F Logs a console warning in development if `name` is missing or the wrong type.\n\u002F\u002F No effect in production, and no compile-time safety — TypeScript (ch. 23) is strictly better\n\u002F\u002F for new projects, but you will encounter PropTypes in real, older codebases.\n",[23,1669,1670,1684,1688,1705,1720,1724,1728,1738,1743,1748,1752,1757,1762],{"__ignoreMap":49},[53,1671,1672,1675,1678,1681],{"class":55,"line":56},[53,1673,1674],{"class":59},"import",[53,1676,1677],{"class":67}," PropTypes ",[53,1679,1680],{"class":59},"from",[53,1682,1683],{"class":114}," 'prop-types'\n",[53,1685,1686],{"class":55,"line":89},[53,1687,212],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":211},[53,1689,1690,1692,1694,1696,1698,1700,1703],{"class":55,"line":98},[53,1691,60],{"class":59},[53,1693,64],{"class":63},[53,1695,68],{"class":67},[53,1697,72],{"class":71},[53,1699,75],{"class":67},[53,1701,1702],{"class":71},"age",[53,1704,86],{"class":67},[53,1706,1707,1709,1711,1713,1716,1718],{"class":55,"line":121},[53,1708,92],{"class":59},[53,1710,403],{"class":67},[53,1712,19],{"class":104},[53,1714,1715],{"class":67},">{name} is {age}\u003C\u002F",[53,1717,19],{"class":104},[53,1719,118],{"class":67},[53,1721,1722],{"class":55,"line":157},[53,1723,205],{"class":67},[53,1725,1726],{"class":55,"line":172},[53,1727,212],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":211},[53,1729,1730,1733,1735],{"class":55,"line":186},[53,1731,1732],{"class":67},"UserCard.propTypes ",[53,1734,111],{"class":59},[53,1736,1737],{"class":67}," {\n",[53,1739,1740],{"class":55,"line":196},[53,1741,1742],{"class":67},"  name: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\n",[53,1744,1745],{"class":55,"line":202},[53,1746,1747],{"class":67},"  age: PropTypes.number,\n",[53,1749,1750],{"class":55,"line":208},[53,1751,205],{"class":67},[53,1753,1754],{"class":55,"line":215},[53,1755,1756],{"class":395},"\u002F\u002F Logs a console warning in development if `name` is missing or the wrong type.\n",[53,1758,1759],{"class":55,"line":582},[53,1760,1761],{"class":395},"\u002F\u002F No effect in production, and no compile-time safety — TypeScript (ch. 23) is strictly better\n",[53,1763,1764],{"class":55,"line":601},[53,1765,1766],{"class":395},"\u002F\u002F for new projects, but you will encounter PropTypes in real, older codebases.\n",[14,1768,1770],{"id":1769},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[1772,1773,1774,1784,1805,1818,1828],"ul",{},[1775,1776,1777,1780,1781,1783],"li",{},[28,1778,1779],{},"Idiom"," — Destructure props directly in the function signature rather than accepting a single ",[23,1782,499],{}," object and dotting into it repeatedly; the signature becomes self-documenting and diffs stay small when a prop is added or removed.",[1775,1785,1786,1789,1790,1792,1793,1795,1796,1798,1799,1801,1802,1804],{},[28,1787,1788],{},"Debug"," — If a prop silently isn't applying its default, check whether the caller is passing ",[23,1791,25],{}," rather than omitting the prop or passing ",[23,1794,923],{}," — default parameters only trigger on ",[23,1797,923],{},", not ",[23,1800,25],{},", and this is a very easy detail to miss when a prop's value comes from an API response that uses ",[23,1803,25],{}," for \"empty.\"",[1775,1806,1807,1809,1810,1813,1814,1817],{},[28,1808,1779],{}," — Pass whole objects (",[23,1811,1812],{},"\u003CProfileLink user={user} \u002F>",") instead of enumerating every field individually (",[23,1815,1816],{},"name={user.name} email={user.email} ...",") when the child genuinely needs most of the object — but do enumerate individual primitive fields when only one or two are used, since that keeps the component's dependency on the parent's shape explicit and easier to memoize (chapter 9).",[1775,1819,1820,1823,1824,1827],{},[28,1821,1822],{},"Performance"," — Spreading unknown extra props onto a DOM element (",[23,1825,1826],{},"\u003Cinput {...rest} \u002F>",") is a common and valid pattern for building wrapper components, but be aware every unrecognized prop that reaches a real DOM element (not a custom component) triggers a React warning and is dropped — filter out non-DOM props before spreading onto host elements.",[1775,1829,1830,1833,1834,1836],{},[28,1831,1832],{},"Portability"," — ",[23,1835,1661],{}," still works in modern React but provides zero compile-time safety and no editor autocomplete; for any project expected to grow past a prototype, TypeScript's prop typing (chapter 23) is the modern default and this curriculum treats PropTypes purely as legacy-literacy.",[14,1838,1840],{"id":1839},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[1772,1842,1843,1853,1865,1882,1904],{},[1775,1844,1845,1848,1849,1852],{},[28,1846,1847],{},"Mutating a prop object mutates the parent's data too"," — objects and arrays passed as props are references, not copies; ",[23,1850,1851],{},"props.items.push(x)"," inside a child silently corrupts the parent's array without React ever knowing a \"change\" happened, since the reference itself didn't change — this can suppress re-renders entirely while also corrupting shared state.",[1775,1854,1855,1860,1861,1864],{},[28,1856,1857,1859],{},[23,1858,679],{}," is deprecated on function components"," — it still executes today, but React 19+ logs a deprecation warning, and a future major version removes support entirely; default parameter destructuring (",[23,1862,1863],{},"({ x = 1 })",") is the forward-compatible replacement and has identical runtime behavior today.",[1775,1866,1867,1833,1870,1873,1874,1877,1878,1881],{},[28,1868,1869],{},"Lowercase component names are silently treated as HTML tags",[23,1871,1872],{},"\u003CuserCard \u002F>"," (lowercase first letter) does not error; JSX treats any lowercase-first tag name as a host element (like ",[23,1875,1876],{},"\u003Cdiv>","), so React tries to render an unknown DOM element ",[23,1879,1880],{},"\u003Cusercard>"," instead of your component, and your props end up as (ignored, with warnings) raw DOM attributes.",[1775,1883,1884,1833,1887,1890,1891,1894,1895,1898,1899,1903],{},[28,1885,1886],{},"Passing a new inline object\u002Farray\u002Ffunction as a prop creates a new reference every render",[23,1888,1889],{},"\u003CWidget style={{ color: 'red' }} \u002F>"," allocates a brand-new object on every parent render, which defeats ",[23,1892,1893],{},"React.memo"," on ",[23,1896,1897],{},"Widget"," (chapter 20) even though the ",[1900,1901,1902],"em",{},"values"," never actually change — the object's identity changes, and memo comparisons are reference-based by default.",[1775,1905,1906,1911,1912,1915,1916,1919,1920,1923,1924,1926],{},[28,1907,1908,1910],{},[23,1909,1054],{}," is not always an array"," — a component with exactly one child receives that child directly (an object or string), not a one-element array; code that assumes ",[23,1913,1914],{},"children.map(...)"," works unconditionally throws ",[23,1917,1918],{},"children.map is not a function"," when there's only a single child. Use ",[23,1921,1922],{},"React.Children.map"," if you must operate on ",[23,1925,1054],{}," generically regardless of count.",[14,1928,1930],{"id":1929},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[19,1932,1933],{},"A settings panel toggles a preference, but sometimes the change appears to \"leak\" into another user's cached card elsewhere on the page.",[41,1935,1936],{"language":43},[45,1937,1939],{"className":47,"code":1938,"language":43,"meta":49,"style":49},"function NotificationSettings({ preferences }) {\n  function toggleEmail() {\n    preferences.email = !preferences.email  \u002F\u002F mutate directly, then force a local re-render\n    forceRerender()\n  }\n\n  return (\n    \u003Clabel>\n      \u003Cinput type=\"checkbox\" checked={preferences.email} onChange={toggleEmail} \u002F>\n      Email notifications\n    \u003C\u002Flabel>\n  )\n}\n",[23,1940,1941,1955,1965,1981,1989,1994,1998,2004,2012,2043,2048,2056,2060],{"__ignoreMap":49},[53,1942,1943,1945,1948,1950,1953],{"class":55,"line":56},[53,1944,60],{"class":59},[53,1946,1947],{"class":63}," NotificationSettings",[53,1949,68],{"class":67},[53,1951,1952],{"class":71},"preferences",[53,1954,86],{"class":67},[53,1956,1957,1960,1963],{"class":55,"line":89},[53,1958,1959],{"class":59},"  function",[53,1961,1962],{"class":63}," toggleEmail",[53,1964,1413],{"class":67},[53,1966,1967,1970,1972,1975,1978],{"class":55,"line":98},[53,1968,1969],{"class":67},"    preferences.email ",[53,1971,111],{"class":59},[53,1973,1974],{"class":59}," !",[53,1976,1977],{"class":67},"preferences.email  ",[53,1979,1980],{"class":395},"\u002F\u002F mutate directly, then force a local re-render\n",[53,1982,1983,1986],{"class":55,"line":121},[53,1984,1985],{"class":63},"    forceRerender",[53,1987,1988],{"class":67},"()\n",[53,1990,1991],{"class":55,"line":157},[53,1992,1993],{"class":67},"  }\n",[53,1995,1996],{"class":55,"line":172},[53,1997,212],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":211},[53,1999,2000,2002],{"class":55,"line":186},[53,2001,92],{"class":59},[53,2003,95],{"class":67},[53,2005,2006,2008,2010],{"class":55,"line":196},[53,2007,101],{"class":67},[53,2009,699],{"class":104},[53,2011,118],{"class":67},[53,2013,2014,2016,2019,2022,2024,2027,2030,2032,2035,2038,2040],{"class":55,"line":202},[53,2015,124],{"class":67},[53,2017,2018],{"class":104},"input",[53,2020,2021],{"class":63}," type",[53,2023,111],{"class":59},[53,2025,2026],{"class":114},"\"checkbox\"",[53,2028,2029],{"class":63}," checked",[53,2031,111],{"class":59},[53,2033,2034],{"class":67},"{preferences.email} ",[53,2036,2037],{"class":63},"onChange",[53,2039,111],{"class":59},[53,2041,2042],{"class":67},"{toggleEmail} \u002F>\n",[53,2044,2045],{"class":55,"line":208},[53,2046,2047],{"class":67},"      Email notifications\n",[53,2049,2050,2052,2054],{"class":55,"line":215},[53,2051,189],{"class":67},[53,2053,699],{"class":104},[53,2055,118],{"class":67},[53,2057,2058],{"class":55,"line":582},[53,2059,199],{"class":67},[53,2061,2062],{"class":55,"line":601},[53,2063,205],{"class":67},[2065,2066,2067,2071,2084],"details",{},[2068,2069,2070],"summary",{},"Answer",[19,2072,2073,2075,2076,2079,2080,2083],{},[23,2074,1952],{}," is an object reference passed down from a parent (likely from some shared cache or context). Mutating ",[23,2077,2078],{},"preferences.email"," directly changes the ",[1900,2081,2082],{},"same object"," that other components — or a cache keyed by that object — are also holding a reference to. Because the mutation doesn't create a new object, any sibling relying on the same reference sees the changed value too, even though it never \"received\" an update through props.",[19,2085,2086,2089,2090,2093],{},[28,2087,2088],{},"The lesson",": never mutate a prop (or any object passed by reference); always derive a new object (",[23,2091,2092],{},"{ ...preferences, email: !preferences.email }",") and pass it up through a callback so the actual owner of the state updates it immutably and re-renders everyone correctly.",[14,2095,2097],{"id":2096},"key-takeaways","Key Takeaways",[1772,2099,2100,2103,2106,2117,2122,2125],{},[1775,2101,2102],{},"Components are functions returning JSX; PascalCase names distinguish custom components from host DOM tags in JSX.",[1775,2104,2105],{},"Props are a read-only, single object argument — never mutate them; derive new values instead.",[1775,2107,2108,2109,2112,2113,2116],{},"Default parameter destructuring (",[23,2110,2111],{},"{ x = 1 }",") is the modern way to set prop defaults; ",[23,2114,2115],{},"defaultProps"," is deprecated.",[1775,2118,2119,2121],{},[23,2120,1054],{}," is a special prop for nested content and is the foundation of the composition patterns in chapter 15.",[1775,2123,2124],{},"Prop drilling — forwarding a value through layers that don't use it — is a naming of a problem, not a pattern to embrace; Context (chapter 7) and composition (chapter 15) are the fixes.",[1775,2126,2127,2128,2130],{},"Inline object\u002Farray\u002Ffunction props create a new reference on every render, which matters once ",[23,2129,1893],{}," enters the picture (chapter 20).",[2132,2133,2134],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sCrzJ, html code.shiki .sCrzJ{--shiki-default:#E36209;--shiki-github-dark:#FFAB70}html pre.shiki code .sk71V, html code.shiki .sk71V{--shiki-default:#22863A;--shiki-github-dark:#85E89D}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-da